WEBVTT

00:05.500 --> 00:07.580
Okay, I'll try and keep up this pace!

00:07.580 --> 00:10.260
Yeah, work hard! Work hard!

00:15.080 --> 00:16.510
I must be tired.

00:16.510 --> 00:19.000
I'm hearing Agate's voice...

00:19.000 --> 00:21.780
Your hard work is paying off.

00:21.780 --> 00:24.120
Is that really you, Agate?

00:24.120 --> 00:25.560
Yes.

00:25.560 --> 00:31.280
Agate lives in the hearts
of her most devout fans.

00:31.280 --> 00:34.260
And I've finally reached that level?!

00:34.260 --> 00:37.240
Now you must continue to buy
all her merchandise forever!

00:39.490 --> 00:43.230
The Agate in my heart is kind of greedy.

00:44.080 --> 00:47.190
You'll wind up out of breath
if you keep running.

00:47.190 --> 00:49.400
Why not take a break?

00:49.400 --> 00:52.950
Y-Yeah. Good idea, Agate...

00:52.950 --> 00:54.480
Agate?!

00:56.200 --> 01:01.400
You're just running around this park with
nowhere else to go, then, Mr. Stray Dog?

01:01.990 --> 01:03.540
Is that what it looked like?

01:04.720 --> 01:07.500
You have some goal, don't you?

01:08.820 --> 01:10.090
Well, I guess so.

01:10.420 --> 01:11.540
I'm glad.

01:11.870 --> 01:15.000
Now I feel a little less guilty.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.160
Guilty?

01:16.460 --> 01:18.270
That's a little much, don't you think?

01:18.270 --> 01:21.910
Yes. I almost killed someone!

01:21.910 --> 01:23.650
That's definitely a little much!

01:25.680 --> 01:29.680
You're not a stray dog at all
anymore, are you, Mr. Stray Dog?

01:30.940 --> 01:34.670
I've been really happy about that.

01:34.670 --> 01:39.320
Sorry. Sometimes, I lose track
of what you're talking about...

01:40.270 --> 01:41.670
Of course.

01:41.670 --> 01:44.890
Well, do you remember the
day I gave you that ticket?

01:44.890 --> 01:48.500
Give me a second so I can get
it all straight in my head!

01:49.550 --> 01:54.100
Once I did, two thoughts went to war in my brain:

01:54.100 --> 01:57.520
that I'm glad I gave it to you, and that
I never should have given it to you.

01:57.520 --> 01:59.620
Oh, I don't mean they literally went to war.

02:00.050 --> 02:00.840
I know that.

02:03.040 --> 02:08.100
And then, the day of the
concert, you showed up.

02:08.320 --> 02:11.340
And the war between
"I'm so glad I gave him the ticket"

02:11.340 --> 02:15.360
and "I never should've given
him that ticket" continued.

02:15.360 --> 02:18.610
I mean, you'd think I'd feel better
after you showed up, right?

02:19.980 --> 02:20.730
Yeah.

02:21.160 --> 02:25.760
The greatest thing for an idol is
for someone to care about you.

02:25.760 --> 02:29.130
But some people take it too far.

02:29.570 --> 02:34.040
If you were that type of person,
instead of helping you feel better,

02:34.040 --> 02:37.310
I was worried I might've
ruined your life for good.

02:37.890 --> 02:42.610
And each time I saw you in the
stands, I kept thinking that...

02:43.890 --> 02:46.620
So I'm glad.

02:47.900 --> 02:50.030
Do you follow me now?

02:52.550 --> 02:57.630
To be honest, if I hadn't become an idol
otaku, I might've chosen another thing.

02:58.150 --> 03:00.650
I might've even become a criminal.

03:01.860 --> 03:06.170
But instead, there was somebody like you
to push me back on the right path.

03:07.960 --> 03:10.410
That's what an idol is.

03:10.780 --> 03:11.910
Huh...

03:11.910 --> 03:12.940
"Huh"?!

03:12.940 --> 03:16.780
No, no! It's a good "Huh".

03:16.780 --> 03:18.170
"Huh".

03:20.420 --> 03:24.680
Talking to you has made me feel
better, Mr. Former Stray Dog.

03:26.040 --> 03:28.260
I'm an idol, you know.

03:28.560 --> 03:29.600
Huh?

03:29.600 --> 03:32.030
I'm an idol, right?

03:34.270 --> 03:37.160
I could tell there was something
bothering her even before that.

03:37.470 --> 03:42.640
She'd canceled all her concerts and
stopped making public appearances.

03:43.990 --> 03:55.800
Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World

05:14.500 --> 05:19.420
"The Beautiful Paladin"

05:21.470 --> 05:24.090
My name is Bell Haggins.

05:24.090 --> 05:27.070
I help out at my boyfriend's bar,

05:27.070 --> 05:29.850
and in my free time, I sing.

05:30.930 --> 05:33.350
Nobody listens to me.

05:34.220 --> 05:38.500
I sing for my own sake.

05:39.690 --> 05:42.180
That was a wonderful song.

05:45.520 --> 05:47.740
R-Right...

05:48.120 --> 05:49.760
Thank you.

05:50.200 --> 05:51.580
But...

05:52.240 --> 05:55.330
you'd do better if you faced
towards the customers.

05:55.920 --> 05:57.290
I see.

05:58.700 --> 06:00.660
My apologies.

06:00.660 --> 06:06.920
I'm Joseph Coleman, a producer
with Jewelry Productions.

06:01.500 --> 06:03.880
Holy Kingdom of Dineez, South Teran, 1-19-10 2F

06:01.500 --> 06:03.880
Jewelry Productions

06:06.920 --> 06:09.270
Let me ask you a question:

06:10.260 --> 06:12.580
would you like to be an idol?

06:14.050 --> 06:18.620
Bell, I told you to kick out
customers if they act weird.

06:18.620 --> 06:20.210
S-Sorry.

06:20.210 --> 06:21.980
My apologies.

06:21.980 --> 06:24.270
You're the owner of this fine establishment?

06:24.270 --> 06:26.910
You don't look like a customer to me.

06:26.910 --> 06:30.040
I've come to recruit her as an idol.

06:30.810 --> 06:31.920
How much?

06:31.920 --> 06:33.020
Donny!

06:33.410 --> 06:37.730
Let's just say it's a world
where dreams come true.

06:39.100 --> 06:40.660
Sounds fun.

06:40.660 --> 06:41.680
Hey...

06:41.940 --> 06:44.880
I hope you'll come to one of our concerts.

06:46.350 --> 06:49.790
Would it be best if I spoke
to the owner from now on?

06:49.790 --> 06:53.040
Yeah. I'm basically her manager.

06:53.040 --> 06:55.800
Man, I can't wait!

06:57.300 --> 06:59.070
I'm so nervous!

07:03.760 --> 07:06.500
This place is incredible...

07:06.500 --> 07:08.950
We've come this far.
Let's have fun before we go home.

07:09.220 --> 07:11.020
Y-Yeah.

07:19.650 --> 07:24.050
Thanks for coming, everyone!

07:25.380 --> 07:30.310
When I was scouted, the feeling
that took root in my heart...

07:30.310 --> 07:32.860
was greed.

07:33.930 --> 07:36.090
I wanted to be like them!

07:36.320 --> 07:39.720
I wanted people to listen
to and enjoy my songs!

07:40.400 --> 07:43.730
I wanted people to accept me.

07:44.150 --> 07:49.250
I was much greedier than I thought I was.

07:55.340 --> 07:57.100
Thank you very much!

07:59.500 --> 08:00.970
You, too?

08:00.970 --> 08:03.240
Then, the three of us are rivals, huh?

08:07.000 --> 08:10.260
The three of us were all
given different names.

08:10.510 --> 08:13.510
We each took the name of a jewel:

08:13.510 --> 08:14.630
Topaz.

08:14.630 --> 08:15.630
Amber.

08:15.630 --> 08:17.640
And I became Agate.

08:18.900 --> 08:22.430
My days as an idol were so wonderful...

08:23.670 --> 08:26.900
And my relationship with
Donny quickly went south.

08:28.310 --> 08:29.770
Hey, Bell...

08:30.810 --> 08:34.590
I hate to ask, but can I have some money?

08:34.590 --> 08:39.290
So when Donny said those words
to me, I wasn't that sad.

08:39.530 --> 08:43.060
The bar's doing that badly?

08:43.060 --> 08:45.040
Just this once.

08:45.040 --> 08:47.030
You've got the money, right?

08:54.050 --> 08:56.720
Um, Donny, I'm...

08:54.900 --> 08:57.690
Good timing, Bell!

08:59.110 --> 09:02.550
The brighter the spotlights
shone down on me as an idol,

09:02.890 --> 09:06.480
the bigger a shadow they cast
over my life with Donny.

09:06.480 --> 09:09.000
Please, Bell! This is the last time!

09:09.000 --> 09:09.930
Again?

09:09.930 --> 09:12.450
This time it'll be fine!
I've got connections!

09:12.930 --> 09:14.320
What do you mean?

09:14.320 --> 09:17.570
Remember that Tigerian that
came to the bar the other day?

09:17.570 --> 09:20.130
He's going to help me out.

09:20.130 --> 09:21.920
And you're going gambling with him?

09:21.920 --> 09:23.350
D-Dumb girl!

09:23.350 --> 09:24.320
It's an investment!

09:24.640 --> 09:27.130
Don't worry. I'll give you back
a dozen times what you lend me.

09:30.890 --> 09:32.800
Thanks so much, Bell...

09:46.640 --> 09:48.490
Hello, Mr. Stray Dog.

09:54.800 --> 09:59.240
Donny, I've got enough money
to support you financially.

09:59.240 --> 10:02.330
And I know you're blowing
your money on gambling.

10:04.000 --> 10:04.870
But...

10:05.280 --> 10:07.710
Is that really what you want?

10:08.400 --> 10:13.030
The dream you shared with me before
was something totally different!

10:10.750 --> 10:13.500
Jewelry Productions Fan Appreciation Event

10:10.750 --> 10:13.500
Starring

10:10.750 --> 10:13.500
Garnet

10:10.750 --> 10:13.500
Amber Agate Topaz

10:10.750 --> 10:13.500
7:00 PM at Southgate Hall

10:13.540 --> 10:16.390
People will come from all over
the country to eat my food!

10:16.390 --> 10:19.900
Broke-ass adventurers and politicians

10:19.900 --> 10:24.580
with pricey tastes will
both be equal before me!

10:24.580 --> 10:28.140
Don't worry! When that happens,
I'll be adding more tables,

10:28.140 --> 10:32.140
but I'll have a stage for you to
sing on in the middle of the place!

10:32.140 --> 10:35.890
We'll bedazzle them with my
cooking and your singing!

10:36.290 --> 10:37.730
It'll be so much fun, don't you think?

10:40.470 --> 10:44.420
And that was the first time I saw him...

10:48.030 --> 10:49.880
So, let's break up, then!

10:50.790 --> 10:53.730
I mean, if you're not part of Masters of War,

10:53.730 --> 10:55.350
you're just a wimpy Swashbuckler.

10:55.350 --> 10:56.490
Wait, Claudine!

10:56.490 --> 10:57.340
Bye.

10:57.660 --> 11:00.920
No... Claudine...

11:05.190 --> 11:08.450
Then it really started to pour.

11:10.960 --> 11:13.070
He didn't even have an umbrella.

11:13.310 --> 11:17.260
He didn't even seem to
realize it was raining.

11:25.200 --> 11:26.870
You're soaked.

11:29.220 --> 11:31.710
Once, Donny had said to me...

11:32.040 --> 11:34.800
I'll let you watch as I win a lot of money!

11:34.800 --> 11:37.270
Then you'll feel a little better, right?

11:37.270 --> 11:39.130
About the future, and stuff.

11:41.260 --> 11:45.360
Those words felt to me like a break-up.

11:45.360 --> 11:48.510
So I went without saying a thing.

11:48.510 --> 11:50.730
I wanted to see for myself, just once.

11:52.420 --> 11:53.420
Yeah...

11:55.030 --> 12:01.370
And on that day in the
casino, I met a goddess.

12:02.560 --> 12:07.500
When Donny was starting
to win, things changed.

12:10.810 --> 12:14.160
She wasn't the goddess.

12:15.030 --> 12:18.640
She was more like the avatar
of gambling itself,

12:19.010 --> 12:24.220
taking all the chips from everyone
there and walking away.

12:25.390 --> 12:28.760
She had her eyes on me the whole time.

12:29.240 --> 12:34.310
If anything, she seemed to have chosen
that table because I was there.

12:34.940 --> 12:39.550
It wasn't Donny or the dealer she
wanted to destroy. It was me.

12:40.240 --> 12:43.330
And when she'd finished
punishing me, she laughed,

12:43.330 --> 12:46.660
satisfied, and disappeared
in a puff of smoke.

12:48.600 --> 12:52.120
The goddess had a sword that
controlled the weather,

12:52.120 --> 12:55.910
and in an instant, she turned
the room into a frozen tundra.

12:56.730 --> 13:00.240
It was a sight that inspired
awe, and even fear.

13:14.830 --> 13:16.450
My paladin...

13:18.960 --> 13:25.380
We've assumed responsibility
for all of your debts.

13:25.780 --> 13:29.330
No one will distract you
from your cooking now.

13:29.720 --> 13:33.670
You may sleep peacefully,
without fear of debt collectors.

13:34.340 --> 13:40.320
But this is also the end of your
relationship with our idol.

13:40.850 --> 13:45.320
Even if you were to somewhere,
someday, see her on the street,

13:45.320 --> 13:48.600
please don't say a word. Just walk by.

13:48.600 --> 13:51.420
Like the other people on the street.

13:51.840 --> 13:53.980
If you fail to do this...

13:54.890 --> 13:57.950
B-Bell, I'm sorry!

13:57.820 --> 14:02.620
Donny, you don't even know this girl.

13:57.950 --> 13:59.060
I didn't mean...

14:02.620 --> 14:07.860
And a stranger has no right to
touch one of our precious jewels.

14:07.860 --> 14:09.750
It's all right, Joseph!

14:09.750 --> 14:11.230
B-Bell!

14:11.800 --> 14:14.610
I'm glad I got your signature
on the documents first.

14:14.970 --> 14:18.360
While you were still
capable of signing them.

14:18.950 --> 14:19.890
Donny...

14:20.370 --> 14:23.880
Your dreams were so innocent and fun.

14:23.880 --> 14:27.750
I wish I could've stood by your
side and listened to them forever.

14:27.750 --> 14:30.660
I was even willing to quit
being an idol for that.

14:31.000 --> 14:34.650
But at some point,
you stopped looking at me.

14:34.650 --> 14:36.190
Bell, I...

14:36.190 --> 14:40.290
At some point, all you were
seeing was the money behind me.

14:41.410 --> 14:45.910
I know you're not actually
that kind of person.

14:45.910 --> 14:50.470
But right now, having me around
just makes your life worse.

14:50.940 --> 14:51.900
Bell...

14:52.660 --> 14:55.690
No, that's not true...

14:55.690 --> 15:00.050
The truth is, I'm just tired
of betting on the dark horse.

15:00.470 --> 15:04.010
The dark horse? That's me?

15:04.010 --> 15:05.110
I'm sorry.

15:06.530 --> 15:08.670
That's pretty damn...

15:11.700 --> 15:13.040
I'm sorry.

15:15.420 --> 15:17.810
It's fine. That's the problem with amateurs.

15:19.560 --> 15:21.150
Listen to me, Bell.

15:21.150 --> 15:26.530
When you're gambling, the minute you
give up, somebody else takes your prize.

15:26.530 --> 15:28.690
I'm afraid you...

15:28.020 --> 15:30.720
Yeah, I know that, Joseph.

15:30.720 --> 15:32.550
I'm not worth that much.

15:32.550 --> 15:37.190
From my perspective, the offer you're
making is too good to be true.

15:37.510 --> 15:41.660
But the way gambling works,

15:41.660 --> 15:44.950
you never know how things'll
go until it's over.

15:45.310 --> 15:46.620
Just you watch, Bell.

15:49.630 --> 15:50.640
Donny.

15:52.690 --> 15:53.820
Take this.

15:54.980 --> 15:58.100
You saw that goddess, too, right?

15:58.410 --> 16:00.610
She'll protect you.

16:02.100 --> 16:03.410
Dumb girl.

16:03.410 --> 16:06.490
Why would you give a gambler
something so scary?

16:07.230 --> 16:10.110
Really? I'm sorry!

16:12.650 --> 16:16.730
Nah, it's ironic. I like that.

16:19.310 --> 16:24.550
We were lucky that he hurt himself
dealing with those drunks.

16:24.550 --> 16:26.870
I never want to do something
scary like that again.

16:27.740 --> 16:29.520
Thank you so much.

16:30.910 --> 16:35.250
Um... the card I just gave him...

16:37.100 --> 16:39.040
"Accept your death".

16:39.700 --> 16:41.890
You've certainly learned to
speak your mind, haven't you?

16:41.890 --> 16:45.450
No! I didn't mean... Jeez!

16:45.870 --> 16:49.540
I never saw him after that.

17:07.170 --> 17:09.920
Celebrating Agate's Comeback
Solo Concert

17:10.320 --> 17:14.700
When Agate announced she was taking
a break, I was sure it was over.

17:14.700 --> 17:17.270
But now she's back, and with a solo concert!

17:20.690 --> 17:23.050
Good evening, everyone!

17:31.120 --> 17:35.280
I know that I might have worried
you when I took that break...

17:35.280 --> 17:36.200
It's okay!

17:36.200 --> 17:37.310
We've been waiting!

17:37.740 --> 17:40.980
What do you think I was doing?

17:40.980 --> 17:42.960
What?

17:42.960 --> 17:44.500
You went home to your parents!

17:44.500 --> 17:45.730
You ate food!

17:45.730 --> 17:46.940
You were asleep the whole time!

17:46.940 --> 17:48.700
You walked the dog!

17:51.350 --> 17:54.860
Actually, I met a goddess!

17:59.520 --> 18:05.250
You remember that sad incident that
took place at the casino, right?

18:06.570 --> 18:13.840
I was nearby, and I saw a knight in
pure white battle the raging monster.

18:16.430 --> 18:20.750
When danger was near, this pure white
knight appeared from within the light,

18:20.750 --> 18:25.240
defeated the bad guy, and left
without giving her name.

18:25.690 --> 18:28.560
Yes... the goddess I saw was...

18:29.240 --> 18:31.500
the legendary paladin!

18:31.500 --> 18:33.140
What?!

18:33.140 --> 18:34.460
That's a big surprise, huh?

18:34.820 --> 18:37.000
Y-Yeah...

18:38.360 --> 18:43.540
I thought to myself that I wanted to
help someone and give them courage,

18:43.540 --> 18:45.190
like she gave to me.

18:45.770 --> 18:48.730
So I wrote this new song, thinking of her,

18:48.730 --> 18:53.780
and hoping that the feelings
inside me can reach all of you.

18:56.770 --> 18:58.420
Listen to my new song.

18:58.420 --> 19:00.290
"The Beautiful Paladin".

19:12.680 --> 19:19.280
Holding my head high into the future

19:19.280 --> 19:24.930
even if it leads beyond the light,

19:25.180 --> 19:30.870
I will keep vowing, I will keep believing.

19:30.870 --> 19:37.740
No matter how dazzling the light may be...

19:37.740 --> 19:39.850
I'll go on!

19:39.850 --> 19:42.670
Idols got their start as bards.

19:43.020 --> 19:48.790
And bards were more than
people who just sang songs.

19:48.790 --> 19:54.040
They traveled and wrote songs of
the things they heard and saw,

19:54.040 --> 19:57.300
of the beautiful and noble
things in this world,

19:57.300 --> 20:00.180
and sometimes of the foolishness of mankind.

20:00.180 --> 20:06.450
My encounter with the paladin made me
realize that I wanted to be a real idol.

20:07.060 --> 20:14.960
I want to be like those bards,
and inspire and encourage people who fight.

20:13.850 --> 20:21.860
Celebrating Agate's Comeback
Solo Concert
South Teran Auditorium Outdoor Stage
Gates 17:30, Start 18:00
Produced by Jewelry Productions

20:27.600 --> 20:30.700
"It feels so good to have a
drink after you exercise.

20:31.800 --> 20:35.080
I think I just heard Agate's voice.

20:35.080 --> 20:37.550
No, no. She must be tired

20:37.550 --> 20:41.460
after her massively successful
comeback concert the other day.

20:41.460 --> 20:46.300
There's no way she'd come
to see a stray dog like me!

20:46.300 --> 20:49.440
Wahaha!"

20:49.440 --> 20:53.210
My internal voice sure likes to prattle on...

20:53.720 --> 20:56.250
"But more importantly, this drink...

20:56.250 --> 21:00.740
This drink is what I live for!"

20:58.890 --> 21:00.540
You okay?

21:00.740 --> 21:03.860
W-With what?

21:03.860 --> 21:07.070
You looked like something was
bothering you last time.

21:08.120 --> 21:10.070
N-Nothing was bothering me...

21:12.240 --> 21:15.230
Worries...

21:16.840 --> 21:20.790
Of course I have worries. I'm human.

21:21.970 --> 21:24.840
You solve one, and then there's another...

21:24.840 --> 21:28.320
Or two or three at the same time...

21:28.910 --> 21:29.830
Yeah.

21:29.830 --> 21:32.710
Or four, or five, or six...

21:33.600 --> 21:36.870
Once you get a taste for them,
it's hard to let go.

21:36.870 --> 21:40.850
That's true for people and
stray dogs both, woof.

21:41.110 --> 21:42.860
You're still doing that?

21:42.860 --> 21:45.460
A stray dog can be strong, too, woof.

21:45.460 --> 21:46.770
I can do this, woof.

21:48.700 --> 21:51.900
Yeah. You gotta.

21:51.900 --> 21:53.380
Woof. Woof.

21:54.030 --> 21:56.390
Whenever you resolve
something that's bothering you,

21:56.390 --> 21:59.370
it means you're taking a step forward.

21:59.850 --> 22:00.740
Yeah.

22:07.080 --> 22:09.640
You gotta move forward.

22:12.910 --> 22:13.740
Woof.

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Next time:
"The Legend of the Labyrinth City - Stepping Man?!"

23:35.910 --> 23:39.700
Next time: "The Legend of the Labyrinth City - Stepping Man?!".
